From 9086a87b204ff6ab60bbed02f298bc529650c0b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:13:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST Economy 0049: the strike owns production, gold,
 research and policy while it's active

The user's structural fix, via the lead: while a strike is active (PREP, BUILDUP or WAR,
until OVER), it owns these decisions, gated at the lowest level, with CP cut out.
New CvPlayer::IsStrikeActive. Per the ownership audit in RESULTS:
- Production:
  - The executor runs in WAR too: every city builds the army, and the capital's list
    stays in PREP and BUILDUP.
  - CvCity::pushOrder: every new choice of an AI strike city (a push that replaces the
    queue) becomes the executor's pick whenever it has one, logged "STRIKE LIST -
    REDIRECT". Appends (operation units), saved re-pushes and humans pass.
- Gold:
  - CvCity::CanBuyPlot: no paid tile.
  - CvMinorCivAI::CanMajorBuyout and CanMajorDiploMarriage: no, while the ban holds
    (IsStrikeNoWonders).
  - CvDeal::IsPossibleToTradeItem: no gold, gold per turn or research agreement from an
    AI strike civ. Peace deals stay War's.
  - IsGoldPurchaseAllowed: WarmongerHurry's settlers-and-siege rule applies to any strike
    civ while active, whatever its role's flags (the user: "NO on strike purchases
    beyond the hurry rules").
- Research: the plan's list in CvTechAI::ChooseNextTech for a free tech too.
- Policy: the plan's first tree while active, even after the book ends at war, and that
  tree is finished (its best adoptable policy first) before a second opens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj2nf4FeZTEHWjvnhhA
